message: "If you use SIR in your work, please cite the software (this record) and the method paper (see preferred-citation)."
type: software
title: "SIR: Isotonic Bliss Synergy Testing for Drug Combinations"
abbreviation: "SIR"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20604671
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20604671"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AsiaeeLab/isosynergy"
keywords:
  - drug combinations
  - drug synergy
  - isotonic regression
  - Bliss independence
  - shape-constrained regression
  - hypothesis testing
  - R package
abstract: >
  SIR tests drug-combination viability matrices relative to Bliss independence
  using isotonic single-agent curves and surfaces. A standardized excess test
  uses a plug-in parametric bootstrap at exact Bliss with two-stage Monte Carlo.
  Companion mean tests, region scans, activity summaries, missing-well and
  replicate handling, and within-family BH screens are provided through an R
  interface to the bundled Python implementation.
